# STAGE 1: GitHub Repository and CI Foundation

## Goal

Make GitHub the canonical source of the project and ensure every change is automatically validated.

## Tasks

### Repository

Prepare the monorepo for GitHub.

Expected high-level structure:

```text
/
├── apps/
│   ├── web/
│   └── api/
├── packages/              # optional shared code later
├── Docs/
├── prisma/ or app-specific Prisma location
├── .github/
│   └── workflows/
├── README.md
├── .gitignore
└── package.json
```

Do not restructure working code unnecessarily.

### GitHub Actions

Create CI triggered on pull requests and pushes to the main development branch.

CI should run, as applicable:

- dependency install
- lint
- type check
- backend tests
- frontend tests
- integration tests that can safely run in CI
- Prisma validation
- production builds

Use dependency caching where appropriate.

Do not put production secrets in GitHub Actions.

### Branch Strategy

Keep it simple:

```text
main
feature/*
fix/*
```

No complicated GitFlow process.

### Documentation

README should include:

- product overview
- architecture
- local setup
- environment setup
- database setup
- testing
- build commands
- monorepo layout

## Exit Criteria

A fresh clone from GitHub can be configured and run using documented commands.

A pull request automatically runs validation.

## Stop After Stage 1

Do not deploy yet.

